            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0553" n="519" xml:id="pg519"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to
                        Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 58.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of. your excellency’s note No. 272, of the 6th instant, relative to
                    the sugar estate “Victoria,” situated in the district of Sagua, in the Island of
                    Cuba. As your excellency therein states that the United States consul-general at
                    Havana will be instructed to treat directly concerning this matter with the
                    Governor-General of the island, I will confine myself to informing your
                    excellency, in reply to your aforesaid note, that I will send it to my
                    Government, to the end that it may take cognizance of the views of the United
                    States Government on the subject.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
